      "**Package component - What to check before booking**\n• Flights: Departure airport, direct or connecting route, baggage and ticket conditions\n• Makkah hotel: Hotel name, room type, star level and practical walking distance to Masjid al-Haram\n• Madinah hotel: Hotel name, room type and location relative to Masjid an-Nabawi\n• Entry/visa support: What the agency handles and what remains your responsibility\n• Transfers: Airport transfer, Makkah–Madinah transport and whether shared or private\n• Ziyarat: Included, optional or charged separately\n• Meals: Breakfast, half-board, full-board or none\n• Room occupancy: Double, triple or quad sharing\n• Financial protection: Whether a qualifying flight-inclusive booking is ATOL protected",
      "Do not compare two packages only by headline price. First make the inclusions comparable. A lower quote can become more expensive if baggage, transfers, meals or a better-located hotel have to be added later.",
      "## How to Compare 3-Star, 4-Star and 5-Star Umrah Packages",
      "Hotel star level affects comfort and often price, but it should not be the only deciding factor. Current package pages commonly separate their offers into 3-star, 4-star and 5-star categories, while location and itinerary can differ significantly within each category.",
      "### 3-star packages",
      "A 3-star Umrah package generally targets travellers who want to control cost and accept simpler accommodation. Ask for the exact hotel name rather than accepting “3-star near Haram” as a complete description.",
      "A hotel can have an acceptable star category yet still involve a tiring walk or shuttle journey for an elderly family member. Distance and transport arrangements therefore deserve as much attention as the star label.",
      "### 4-star packages",
      "A 4-star package can suit families who want better room standards or a more convenient location without paying for the highest hotel tier.",
      "Compare breakfast, room size, lifts, transport and actual location rather than assuming every 4-star option provides the same experience.",
      "### 5-star packages",
      "A 5-star Umrah package is most useful when the extra cost buys practical convenience. A closer hotel, suitable room configuration, private transport or a better flight itinerary can reduce fatigue.",
      "Premium branding alone does not guarantee that the package is right for your group. Travellers considering premium accommodation can also compare Haram Trip’s guidance on 5-star luxury Umrah packages from the UK.",
      "## Trip Length and the Makkah–Madinah Split",
      "Umrah packages from the UK are sold in different durations, and the best length depends on available leave, budget, health and preferred pace. Seven-, ten-, twelve- and fourteen-night options appear frequently across current commercial pages, although individual providers offer different combinations.",
      "A shorter itinerary can suit travellers with limited time, while a longer stay can give families and older pilgrims more time to rest between travel and worship.",
      "The total number of nights is only half the question. Ask how those nights are divided between Makkah and Madinah.",
      "Two packages with the same total duration may feel very different if one gives more nights in Makkah and the other provides an even split. Also check whether travel days are counted as package days, because that changes how much usable time you have in each city.",
      "Hotel location also deserves closer inspection. Haram Trip’s Makkah hotel options can help travellers understand the accommodation side of the journey before comparing a complete package.",
      "## Flights From the UK: Compare the Whole Journey",
      "Flights are one of the biggest practical differences between Umrah packages from UK providers. Do not compare only the departure airport or airfare. Check departure time, connection length, baggage allowance, arrival airport, onward transfer and return itinerary.",
      "Current UK package pages advertise both direct and connecting arrangements and departures from several major UK cities, but the exact route depends on travel date and provider.",
      "A connecting flight can offer different schedule or pricing options, but it adds another airport, another boarding process and more travel time. A more convenient itinerary may be worth paying for when travelling with young children, elderly parents or passengers who need assistance.",
      "### Umrah packages from Birmingham",
      "For travellers in Birmingham and the West Midlands, starting at Birmingham Airport can reduce the UK road or rail journey before the international flight. That convenience should still be compared against the actual itinerary.",
      "Ask the agency to show the full route, airline, baggage, connection time and Saudi arrival airport. If London or Manchester is offered as an alternative, include the cost of getting there, parking, a possible airport hotel and the extra travel time.",
      "The best Umrah packages from Birmingham are therefore not simply packages with “BHX” in the advert. The better choice is the itinerary that works for the people travelling.",
      "Haram Trip also has a dedicated Birmingham Umrah travel agency guide covering package inclusions, agency checks and departure considerations.",
      "### Other UK departure points",
      "Travellers using London, Manchester, Glasgow, Edinburgh or other airports should use the same method.",
      "Compare the full door-to-hotel journey rather than the flight price alone. Route availability changes, so verify the actual flight details for your intended travel date before paying.",
      "## Visa, Nusuk and Health Checks for 2026",
      "Saudi entry and pilgrimage rules can change, so check official guidance for your passport and travel date before departure.",
      "GOV.UK Saudi Arabia entry requirements currently state that eligible travellers can use Saudi Arabia’s electronic travel authorisation for Umrah outside the Hajj season. Hajj has separate visa requirements.",
      "Do not assume every UK resident follows the same process. Nationality, passport and visa category can affect eligibility.",
      "The Saudi Ministry of Hajj and Umrah’s calendar for the 1448 AH season confirms the use of the Nusuk application for issuing Umrah permits. Before travelling, check official Saudi channels rather than relying on an old agency page or saved screenshot.",
      "Health requirements deserve the same attention. Current GOV.UK pilgrimage guidance states that Hajj and Umrah travellers need a valid certificate of vaccination against the ACWY strains of meningitis at least 10 days before arrival. Recheck the health requirements close to your departure because official rules may change.",
      "## How ATOL Protection Applies to Umrah Packages",
      "ATOL is financial protection for qualifying flight-inclusive package bookings; it is not travel insurance. The scheme is operated by the UK Civil Aviation Authority (CAA).",
      "Before paying, use the CAA ATOL checker to verify the travel company and its ATOL number. Do not rely only on an ATOL logo displayed on a website.",
      "When an ATOL-protected trip is booked, the CAA says the customer should receive an ATOL Certificate when money is paid, including when the first payment is only a deposit. The certificate states what is protected, who is covered and which ATOL holder provides the protection.",
      "Travel insurance is separate. Choose a policy suitable for your medical needs, itinerary and cancellation risks.",
      "## Which Umrah Package Fits Your Group?",
      "Families should prioritise room configuration, baggage, transfer simplicity and realistic walking distances. A cheaper quad-sharing arrangement may suit one family but be uncomfortable for another.",
      "Older pilgrims and travellers with limited mobility should ask about lifts, hotel access, wheelchair arrangements, transport drop-off points and the practical route to Masjid al-Haram or Masjid an-Nabawi.",
      "Group travellers should confirm who leads the group, what support is available in Saudi Arabia, whether Ziyarat is fixed or optional, and how much flexibility exists if somebody needs rest.",
      "Solo travellers should pay close attention to room-sharing rules and single supplements. Ask for the final room arrangement before paying a deposit.",
      "## A Simple Quote Comparison Checklist",
      "Use the same checklist for every agency so attractive wording does not hide a weaker itinerary.",
      "**Compare - Questions to ask**\n• Total price: What is included, excluded and still payable later?\n• Flights: Which airport, airline, route and baggage allowance?\n• Makkah stay: Which hotel, room type and number of nights?\n• Madinah stay: Which hotel, room type and number of nights?\n• Hotel access: What is the practical route to the mosque?\n• Transfers: Shared or private? Airport and intercity included?\n• Visa/permit help: What does the provider do and what must I do?\n• Ziyarat: Included, optional or extra?\n• Meals: Which meals are included?\n• Protection: Is the flight-inclusive booking ATOL protected?\n• Terms: What are the change and cancellation conditions?",
      "When you have those answers in writing, labels such as “economy”, “premium” and “all-inclusive” become much easier to judge.",
      "## Choosing Umrah Packages 2026 with Confidence",
      "The right Umrah package is the one that fits your people, not the one with the loudest discount.",
      "Compare flights, hotel names, distance, room occupancy, nights in each city, transfers, travel-document support and financial protection before deciding.",
      "For pilgrims researching current options, Haram Trip provides UK Umrah package information and package choices. Use live package details as a starting point, then confirm the exact quotation for your dates and departure city.",
      "For 2026 travel, check official Saudi and UK guidance again before departure. A well-chosen package should reduce practical uncertainty so you can give more attention to the purpose of the journey itself."
