      "## Why December Draws So Many UK Pilgrims",
      "Three things line up in December that don’t line up for the rest of the year.",
      "The first is the weather. Saudi Arabia’s summer heat, often above 40°C, makes long hours at the Haram genuinely difficult. December temperatures typically sit between 15°C and 28°C during the day, which makes Tawaf, Sa’i, and extended prayer far more manageable, particularly for children and older relatives.",
